# model-server — copy to .env

# Which slots run (slot names, not model names).
COMPOSE_PROFILES=tts

# Folder name under stt/, tts/, or llm/ for each slot.
STT_MODEL=
TTS_MODEL=orpheus
LLM_MODEL=

# GPU index(es). On ace-h200 use 1 (GPU 0 is production).
GPU_DEVICE_IDS=0

# A gRPC front door for the STT slot, for callers that cannot hold a WebSocket
# (NVIDIA Cloud Functions has no WebSocket invocation path). UNSET IS OFF, and
# off is total: compose-files.sh does not name compose.grpc.yml, so the
# resolved config is identical to one from before the facade existed.
#
# It was missing from this file entirely, so a fresh checkout had no way to
# know the option existed and start-model-server.sh now asks instead.
USE_STT_GRPC=

# Only published port; model containers bind nothing on the host.
GATEWAY_PORT=8100

# Upstreams default to Compose service names. Uncomment to override.
# STT_UPSTREAM=http://stt:8001
# TTS_UPSTREAM=http://tts:8002
# LLM_UPSTREAM=http://llm:8003

# Weights (paths inside the container).
INDIC_NEMO_PATH=/app/models/IndicConformer.nemo
BHILI_ENABLE=no
BHILI_NEMO_PATH=

# HuggingFace cache / token (gated Parler tokenizer).
HF_CACHE_VOLUME=voicera-prod_hf_cache
HF_TOKEN=

# A token for one slot only, used in place of HF_TOKEN for that slot and
# nothing else. Leave them empty and every slot uses HF_TOKEN, which is what
# one account's token already covers.
#
# They exist for the two cases a single token cannot express: access to the
# gated repos granted to different HuggingFace accounts, and fine-grained
# tokens scoped to one repository each. start-model-server.sh offers the
# choice and writes whichever you pick here.
#
# The fallback is Compose's, not the script's -- each service resolves
# ${<SLOT>_HF_TOKEN:-${HF_TOKEN:-}} -- so an .env written before these existed
# behaves exactly as it did, and a stack driven by hand needs no new keys.
# The TTS value also reaches indic-mio's vLLM sidecar, which fills that slot.
STT_HF_TOKEN=
TTS_HF_TOKEN=
LLM_HF_TOKEN=

# vLLM limits for the LLM slot.
VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
VLLM_MAX_NUM_SEQS=20
# Keep low on shared MPS GPUs (default 0.9 would starve other workers).
VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.10
# Empty means bf16.
VLLM_QUANTIZATION=

# Local AI4Bharat NeMo fork (build context). Only stt/indic-conformer's
# Dockerfile uses it -- `COPY --from=nemo` -- but Compose stats every declared
# build context whether or not a Dockerfile references it, so this must name a
# directory that EXISTS even when the selected model has no use for it.
#
# start-model-server.sh handles that: it clones the fork for indic-conformer,
# and points this at an empty placeholder for everything else. Set it by hand
# only when driving Compose without the script.
#
# This shipped as /home/kowshik/ai4bharat_nemo -- one person's home directory,
# so every fresh checkout inherited a path that existed on exactly one machine
# and failed the build with "failed to get build context nemo".
#
# git clone --branch nemo-v2 --depth 1 https://github.com/AI4Bharat/NeMo.git ~/ai4bharat_nemo
NEMO_CONTEXT_PATH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tts/rumik-oss-1 (Rumik OSS-1, 3B + Mimi codec)
#
# Every key below is declared in tts/rumik-oss-1/compose.extra.yml, which is
# what actually passes it into the container; this block is so an operator can
# discover that it exists. Commented means "the compose default applies" --
# uncomment only what this deployment needs to change.
#
# LICENCE: CC-BY-NC-4.0 with an acceptable-use addendum. Research and
# non-commercial use only. A commercial deployment needs separate permission
# from Rumik. See tts/rumik-oss-1/README.md.

# Which backend produces tokens: vllm (default) or transformers. The
# transformers path runs the checkpoint's own per-token Python loop, measured at
# ~45 tok/s against the 100 tok/s a single realtime stream needs; vLLM exists to
# fix that. Kept selectable so the two can be compared.
# RUMIK_ENGINE=vllm
# RUMIK_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
# vLLM reserves this FRACTION OF THE CARD'S TOTAL at startup and holds it
# whether it needs it or not. 0.12 is ~17 GB of a 143 GB H200 and matches what
# orpheus settled on for a 3B model on the same card.
# RUMIK_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.12
# vLLM's batch ceiling, distinct from RUMIK_MAX_CONCURRENCY (the slot's
# admission limit).
# RUMIK_MAX_NUM_SEQS=64
# CUDA graphs are most of the speedup; only disable them to debug capture.
# RUMIK_ENFORCE_EAGER=false

# Where fetch.sh put the checkpoint, as the host sees it. Mounted read-only at
# /models in the container.
# RUMIK_MODELS_DIR=./tts/rumik-oss-1/models
# A directory under that mount, or a HuggingFace repo id (which makes the load
# download into HF_HOME instead -- do not combine that with HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1).
# RUMIK_MODEL_PATH=/models/rumik-oss-1
# Reported at /v1/models and /health. Keep it equal to the folder and catalogue
# id, or an agent asking for this model by name reaches nothing.
# RUMIK_MODEL_NAME=rumik-oss-1
# RUMIK_DEVICE=cuda
# bfloat16 is what the checkpoint was saved in. float16 loads and quietly
# changes the audio.
# RUMIK_DTYPE=bfloat16
# RUMIK_ATTN_IMPLEMENTATION=sdpa

# Concurrent synthesis limit. 1 ON PURPOSE, and measured: no continuous
# batching -- generation is a per-token Python loop over a 3B model -- so a
# single stream already runs at RTF ~2.2 and underruns. Two makes it ~4.4.
# Each stream also holds ~1.2 GB of KV cache at the full context. Raise it only
# with an X-RTF under 1.0 in hand.
# RUMIK_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1
# RUMIK_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=1000

# RUMIK_HOST=0.0.0.0
# RUMIK_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# RUMIK_CORS_ORIGINS=

# Ira, Aisha, Siya, Zoya. Unlike Orpheus, the voice does NOT pick the language:
# every voice covers all 22.
# RUMIK_DEFAULT_VOICE=Ira
# The delivery description every caller gets unless it sends `instructions`:
# emotion, accent and pace, comma-separated, e.g. "neutral, steady pace".
# Empty means no <description=...> prefix at all, which is not the same thing
# as an empty one -- the model would condition on that.
# RUMIK_DEFAULT_INSTRUCTIONS=
# The model card's own sampling values. Changing these changes the voice.
# RUMIK_TEMPERATURE=0.8
# RUMIK_TOP_K=30
# RUMIK_MIN_NEW_TOKENS=8
# Eight tokens make one 80 ms frame, so 2048 is ~20 s of speech. Also bounded at
# request time by what is left of the 8192-position context after the prompt.
# RUMIK_MAX_NEW_TOKENS_DEFAULT=2048
# RUMIK_MAX_NEW_TOKENS_LIMIT=2048

# Streaming decode. Chunk is how much audio is emitted at a time (2 frames =
# 160 ms); context is the left window each chunk is decoded with, because Mimi
# in transformers carries no streaming state between calls. Too little context
# is a click at every chunk boundary, not an error.
# RUMIK_DECODE_CHUNK_FRAMES=2
# RUMIK_DECODE_CONTEXT_FRAMES=32
# RUMIK_DECODER_DEVICE=cuda

# One short synthesis at startup, which also proves the sampling tap that
# streaming and cancellation depend on is still wired. Disabling it moves that
# check to the first real request, where a broken tap looks like a wedged GPU.
# RUMIK_WARMUP_ENABLED=true
# 256, not 32: the first generation after a cold context runs at 12.5 tok/s
# and settles at ~45 by the second, so too small a warmup bills the first
# caller for it.
# RUMIK_WARMUP_TOKENS=256

# Two lines used to sit here, uncommented, from an old native-mode run: a
# RUN_MODE set to dev, and
#
#   TTS_UPSTREAM=http://127.0.0.1:8002
#
# Inside the gateway container 127.0.0.1 is the gateway, so that upstream sent
# every TTS request to a port nothing was listening on and /health reported
# "All connection attempts failed" for a tts container that was up and serving.
# The correct forms are commented out near the top of this file: the gateway
# reaches the slots by Compose service name, and leaving the variables unset is
# what selects that. RUN_MODE was read by nothing at all.
